Z||000018||Raydar||10-18-2000||05:52 PM||||KRM, I used to think the 2.5 Duke was based on a Chevy block. (We usta have a MerCruiser 120 that was a 2.5 Chevy 4-banger.) <BR>I was told that that's not the case.<BR>If you look at the GM 3.0 engine (Look at the 2.5 vs 3.0 thread), the head is not a crossflow like ours, and the tranny bolt pattern looks like a Chevy. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Pontiaddict||10-18-2000||06:16 PM||||3 words for ya...<P>Chrysler turbine engine!<P>or<P>Top fuel hemi<P>Sorry, those are PT Cruiser swaps.<P>If you see a 'Cruiser that's making a weird noise (other than it's normal weird  4 banger noise) or shooting flames from zoomies, DON'T RACE IT!<P>Saleen, It's easy to check to see if you car is actually a McLaren F1 with the cool Fiero body kit.<BR>1- look for carbon fiber <BR>2- is the steering wheel in the middle of the car? <BR>3- you can't always look for the v-12 in the back since some of them were swapped out for the ever powerful, often feared 2.8L GM v6.||||reg||1
